@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+---
+id: task-002-correct-order-discount-coupon-expiry-and-shipping-vat
+type: task
+title: "Correct order discount, coupon expiry, and shipping VAT"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+Correct three reported order-pricing defects.
+
+Investigation found that percentage coupons are calculated from the gross order total instead of the
+subtotal after volume discounts; coupon expiry rejects the stated final valid day; and delivery VAT
+is included in pricing, receipts, invoices, and the documented business rules.
+
+The delivery-VAT policy change was approved in `dl-001-treat-delivery-as-vat-exempt` with the reply
+"Approved. Proceed." Implementation is complete:
+
+- Percentage coupons now use the subtotal after volume discounts. Twelve €5.00 notebooks with a
+  10% coupon yield €48.60 of goods; the existing 50% combined-discount cap remains in force.
+- Coupon validity includes both boundary days, including coupons valid for a single day.
+- Delivery VAT is zero, receipts omit its VAT line, and invoice VAT summaries contain goods only.
+  Invoice totals still include delivery. `shippingVatCents` is retained at zero for compatibility.
+- README rules now describe the approved delivery-VAT policy and invoice behaviour.
+
+Verification classified the reported defects and revised VAT behaviour as red-first criteria; the
+combined-discount cap and free-delivery invoice checks characterize existing behaviour. Before the
+implementation, six regression tests failed for the expected reasons. After implementation, all 23
+tests passed (`npm test`), including boundary dates, discount stacking, paid/free delivery, receipts,
+and invoice totals. `git diff --check` passed. No new dependencies were introduced.
